OpenWings patch 0005: per-agent tool access

Upstream agents (persona presets) carry instructions, temperature and persona
memory but no tool restriction: chat tool access is decided only by per-turn
toggles and the global admin denylist. This adds an optional enabled_tools
list of tool families to each persona (saved templates and the active custom
preset). When set, every tool outside those families, including MCP tools, is
added to the turn's disabled-tool set in routes/chat_routes.py, the same
server-side choke point the global denylist uses (wings/agent_tools.py).
null = no restriction, [] = no tools. Re-posts of the active persona that
omit the field keep the saved value, so they can never widen an agent's
tools. The persona editor gets a 'Tool access' section
(static/js/wings-agent-tools.js); GET /api/tools also lists the families.

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later (same as upstream)

